+## 4. Provenance issue: verified and narrowly remediated
+
+### Finding at HEAD
+
+- **[Verified—checkout]** `src/services/knowledge/provenance/registry.ts` did not declare `first-party:kanji-corpus:v1` as a canonical source, while `SOURCE_ALIASES` mapped that exact identifier to `upstream:kanjidic2:2024-07`.
+- `src/etl/kanji/fixture.ts` marks each of the 12 pilot Kanji as `first-party:kanji-corpus:v1`; `canonicalDataset.ts` likewise records the corpus as first party. Thus `getRegisteredSource()` could return an upstream KANJIDIC2 contract for a first-party record.
+- The same missing identity/alias could produce the same misresolution for callers of `ProvenanceService.assertIngestible()` and `resolveProvenance()`.
+- `src/etl/kanji/loader.ts::ensureKanjiSource()` also described its source row as “KANJIDIC2 / KanjiVG Approved Corpus,” assigned version `2026.1`, a CC BY-SA 3.0 license string and KANJIDIC2 URL, and an upstream-size `recordCount` of 13,108. Those values did not describe the 12-record first-party pilot.
+- `upstream:kanjidic2:2024-07` is registered and remains a separate upstream identity. It is **not** an alias for the first-party corpus after this correction.
+
+### Existing/persisted-data risk
+
+- **[Documented—historical]** `reports/gates/PHASE-14.4C-CONTROLLED-VERIFICATION.md` describes a legacy `knowledge_sources` state with six rows and `first-party:kanji-corpus:v1` `record_count=13,108`. That record was not queried in this session and its present-day existence is unverified.
+- The code correction intentionally does not update/delete any stored row. `ensureKanjiSource()` now inserts the correct first-party metadata when absent and refuses a metadata mismatch when a row already exists, instead of silently accepting it. If a legacy row exists, ingestion must stop; a separate, authorized read-only audit and reviewed data remediation are required.
+- The audit scanned current registry aliases and code references for the identity. No other current `SOURCE_ALIASES` mapping for it remains. Historical reports and prior patch artifacts are records of the old bug, not active runtime mappings.
+
+### Changes made
+
+1. Added an explicit first-party `first-party:kanji-corpus:v1` source entry in `src/services/knowledge/provenance/registry.ts`, with first-party attribution/license language, null URI, Kanji domain and the three canonical target tables.
+2. Removed the erroneous mapping from `SOURCE_ALIASES`. No alternate upstream alias was added.
+3. Corrected `ensureKanjiSource()` in `src/etl/kanji/loader.ts` to identify the 12-headword first-party pilot; it now rejects conflicting existing metadata rather than silently reusing it. It does not modify existing rows.
+4. Added `tests/kanji-corpus-provenance.test.ts` to prove the registry identity, no alias collision, resolution of all 12 pilot records to the corpus identity, and preservation of all 33 Mind Tree identities.
