+### 6.3 Japanese-language fidelity requirements
+
+Preserve separate evidence layers: (1) KANJIDIC2 meanings/readings/grade/stroke/radical index, (2) JMdict lexical written forms/readings/sense glosses/POS/restrictions, (3) KanjiVG literal SVG groups/path order/annotations, (4) editorial visual component and semantic/phonetic interpretation, and (5) pedagogical mnemonics. A Kangxi/classical radical number is not a component identity. A visual primitive is not necessarily a radical. A KanjiVG `kvg:radical`/`kvg:phon` annotation is not proof of historical etymology or modern semantic role. On/Kun/Nanori readings belong to individual Kanji source records; a word’s reading belongs to a JMdict written-form/reading association. Unknown, unavailable, not applicable, and not reviewed must not collapse to a guessed string or invented enum value.
