+# K0.11 — Source Authorization, Provenance Readiness & K0.10 Integration Recovery
+
+**Verdict: BLOCKED.** The repository supports a documented technical source inventory and a fail-closed provenance-readiness check, but the reviewed evidence does not clear any source-derived Kanji field or Mind Tree relationship for new use or learner delivery. Source capability is recorded separately from permission. UNKNOWN remains blocked; no rights or owner decisions were changed.
+
+## 1. Scope, method, and authority boundary
+
+This is a read-only evidence reconciliation plus a standalone readiness verifier. It uses the current K0.4A source lock, K0.5A/B rights controls, K0.8 owner/source decisions, K0.9 implementation decisions, K0.10 machine evidence and narrative, existing contracts/schemas, and file identity metadata. The machine-readable source/field/relationship inventory is [`PHASE-K0.11-SOURCE-AUTHORIZATION-READINESS.json`](PHASE-K0.11-SOURCE-AUTHORIZATION-READINESS.json).
+
+No source corpus was parsed. In particular, the workbook cells were not opened; Tatoeba LFS objects were not fetched or unpacked; JMdict, KANJIDIC2, and KanjiVG source bytes were not acquired; and no book/OCR content was available or used. The workbook’s SHA-256 was checked only as byte identity. Registry `active` labels, hashes, public availability, technical validators, source notices, and synthetic test events are not treated as legal clearance. No commercial reuse permission is established.
+
+No production or nonproduction database/CMS was accessed. No import, seed update, draft, migration, canonical write, publication, deployment, commit, push, merge, source-lock change, rights clearance, or owner-decision change occurred. The five K0.9 shells remain seed intent, not persisted CMS drafts.
+
+## 2. K0.10 narrative and machine-evidence reconciliation
+
+The current K0.10 narrative hash is `687db394dc822dd00dc839260fedb67cb0681d1a4edf67629e293a125edadc79`; the machine JSON hash is `37024b4eae28344542a1f124ec832e42bbe12ed435747ab4ddd12a583125b7c1`. The K0.10 evidence labels all six runs `SYNTHETIC_SOFTWARE_PATH_ONLY`, sets `sourceUsed` to `null`, and states that no authentic source was used.
