+# K0.14 Data Accuracy Report
+
+**Accuracy conclusion: not established.** The checks below establish reproducible source identity and structural observations for a limited OpenJLPT grammar seed only. They do not establish grammar correctness, meaning equivalence, JLPT level accuracy, example naturalness, authorship, copyright/attribution clearance at example level, or suitability for learners. All 100 source records remain unreviewed.
+
+## Evidence and bounded observations
+
+| Check | Result | What the result does—and does not—mean |
+|---|---|---|
+| Immutable source identity and source package integrity | Five grammar files plus license, notice and two READMEs pinned to commit `c42fd9fa3777bfc1775446f7c418d549dfd6e4cf`; byte count, Git blob and SHA-256 checked for each artifact | Confirms these local bytes match the pinned GitHub content identity; does not certify upstream authorship, accuracy or project use rights |
+| JSON parsing | 100 records parsed | Syntax only |
+| Required top-level shape | 100 records have `pattern`, `level`, `meaning`, `formation`, `examples`, `tags` | Field presence only; not completeness or correctness of claims |
+| File/level consistency | 20 records per N1–N5 file; 100 values match file level | Does not certify official JLPT membership or level fit |
+| Examples | 200 `{ja,en}` objects, two per record, both strings nonempty | Does not certify naturalness, grammatical fit, translation equivalence, source origin, or reuse conditions |
+| Tags | 160 tag items; 100 distinct nonempty tag values | Descriptive-source count only; not validated categorization |
+| Structural rejection | 0 rejected; 100 structurally valid | Valid under the implemented local schema, not under a linguistic or canonical product standard |
+| Duplicate checks | 0 exact duplicate records; 1 normalized pattern-key collision, retained | Collision requires human interpretation; no automatic deletion or merge |
+| Human review | 0 reviewed; 100 pending | No human correctness or approval claim |
+| Semantic/linguistic review | Not performed | Accuracy remains unknown |
+| Example/source cross-reference | 0 source IDs/links observed or resolved | No attribution or lineage inferred |
+
+The duplicate collision is between `olp-v0.2.0-n4-0010` and `olp-v0.2.0-n3-0019` after NFC normalization and outer-whitespace trimming. It remains in the normalized output, duplicate diagnostic and review queue. The source does not provide author/source lineage per entry or per-example origin, so those are flagged as unresolved provenance rather than supplied with guessed values.
+
+## Review control
+
+`data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/build/review-queue.json` contains one pending item per source record. The queue asks a qualified reviewer to check meaning, formation, level fit, naturalness, example fit and attribution; source-record evidence includes exact artifact path/hash and locator. There is no reviewer, timestamp, approval, expected correction or publication state other than pending/not authorized. The queue itself is an operational aid and is not evidence that review occurred.
+
+## Broader family accuracy status
+
+No K0.14 source rows were newly acquired or validated for JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KanjiVG, Tatoeba or Japanese WordNet. Their historical source counts and bounded slices remain historical or pre-existing evidence, not fresh accuracy results. Tatoeba's full LFS objects are absent. Idiom/proverb and collocation sources have not been pinned. Existing source-specific restrictions remain unchanged. No `data/research/kanji-radicals/kanji_radicals.xlsx` cells were read.
+
+## Sign-off
+
+- Structural ETL checks: passed for 100 OpenJLPT records.
+- Linguistic/semantic accuracy: **not reviewed / unknown**.
+- Per-entry authorship and per-example provenance: **unknown/not supplied**.
+- Human editorial approval: **none**.
+- Product/publication authorization: **not authorized**.
