+# K0.14 Dataset Materialization Report
+
+**Decision: BLOCKED for canonical/application integration, publication, and production.** A bounded, reproducible, noncanonical local grammar materialization was completed for the pinned OpenJLPT v0.2.0 grammar-only seed. It is an engineering proof of ETL and review-queue mechanics, not project/source approval, production readiness, linguistic accuracy, or learner content authorization. K0.13 remains **BLOCKED**; all earlier source-specific restrictions and Tatoeba sub-gates remain unchanged.
+
+## Scope and safeguards
+
+- Prioritized JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KanjiVG, OpenJLPT, Tatoeba and Japanese WordNet, followed by idioms/proverbs and collocations.
+- Inspected the dirty worktree and existing integration contracts first. The branch was already carrying 98 modified tracked paths and 79 untracked paths before K0.14 additions; this work did not edit any pre-existing tracked path or untracked file.
+- Materialized only the five OpenJLPT grammar JSON files and their license/notice/readme artifacts, pinned to commit `c42fd9fa3777bfc1775446f7c418d549dfd6e4cf`. Local source and output files reside under Git-ignored `data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/`.
+- No JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KanjiVG, Tatoeba or Japanese WordNet source rows were newly acquired, parsed, retained, or analyzed. The five Tatoeba paths in `data/tatoeba/` are Git LFS pointer text, not archives.
+- No database/CMS was accessed. No migrations, seeds, canonical writes, loader calls, API publication, learner/public delivery, or production authorization occurred. No tracked or pre-existing work was reset, cleaned, stashed, overwritten, or removed.
+- No cells in `data/research/kanji-radicals/kanji_radicals.xlsx` were read.
+
+## K0.14 progress counts (not project totals)
+
+| Family | Target | K0.14 source rows actually available to this work | K0.14 local materialized / normalized | Structural checks passed | Human-reviewed | Newly integrated | Current database count |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| Vocabulary / JMdict | 250,000 | 0 newly acquired; current source count unknown | 0 new | 0 new | 0 new | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Kanji facts / variants | 13,000 | 0 newly acquired; historic KANJIDIC2 source count 13,108 is not current K0.14 ingestion | 0 new | 0 new | 0 new | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Kanji graphical assets | Included in 13,000 family target; no separate target | 0 newly acquired; historic KanjiVG count 11,658 is not current K0.14 ingestion | 0 new | 0 new | 0 new | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Sentences / translations | 1,000,000 | 0 source rows; five unmaterialized LFS object pointers | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Grammar | 10,000 | 100 OpenJLPT seed records | 100 raw/local; 100 normalized intermediate | 100 structurally valid | 0; 100 pending | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Idioms / proverbs | 30,000 | No pinned source rows acquired; total unknown | 0 new | 0 new | 0 new | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Collocations | 50,000 | No pinned source rows acquired; total unknown | 0 new | 0 new | 0 new | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Japanese WordNet | Not a substitute for another target | 0; candidate asset not downloaded | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+| Mind Tree relationships | No numeric target specified | 0 new relation rows | 0 new edges | 0 new edges | 0 | 0 | Unknown; not queried |
+
+Historical source/report counts are evidence about earlier reports only. JMdict 206,717, KANJIDIC2 13,108 and KanjiVG 11,658 are not asserted as K0.14 source files, current materialization, current validation, or database integration. The complete family-by-family inventory, existing artifact identities, LFS pointer metadata, quality limits and explicit unknowns are in `PHASE-K0.14-DATASET-INVENTORY.json`.
+
+## OpenJLPT result
+
+- Five immutable grammar source files, total 43,686 bytes; 100 records, 20 per N1–N5 level. Including license, notice and two README files, nine source-package artifacts total 75,135 bytes were acquired and verified against Git blob IDs and SHA-256 hashes. Exact manifest: `data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/source/acquisition-manifest.json`.
+- Local derived outputs: 100 parsed, 100 structurally valid, 100 normalized; 0 rejected; 0 exact duplicate records; one NFC/outer-trim normalized pattern-key collision across N4/N3, retained and reported; 100 review queue entries; 0 completed human reviews; 0 linguistic/semantic claims validated; 0 source cross-references.
+- All 100 records have the six observed fields (`pattern`, `level`, `meaning`, `formation`, `examples`, `tags`), and the 200 examples have nonempty `ja` and `en` values. This is shape/content-presence evidence only, not correctness, naturalness, pedagogical fit, copyright clearance per example, or a source-origin finding.
+- Field-level provenance links each materialized field to the pinned source version, artifact/hash, record locator, source field, and original/normalized value. Per-entry author/source lineage and per-example origin are unavailable.
+- Every review item is explicitly `PENDING`, has no reviewer or timestamp, has no fabricated correction, carries its source locator/hash evidence and review reason codes, and has publication status `NOT_AUTHORIZED`.
+- OpenJLPT's captured repository license declares CC BY-SA 4.0 with attribution, change-indication and ShareAlike conditions and applicable upstream obligations. This local technical use does not establish a NihongoBridge product decision. Publication/production authorization remains `NOT_AUTHORIZED`.
+- Canonical grammar mapping is intentionally absent: OpenJLPT does not supply required canonical fields such as title, structure, explanation and common mistakes. No defaults or values were invented; the canonical loader was not invoked.
+
+## Technical result and remaining gate
+
+The independent Python ETL and its four focused unit tests pass. Two build/verify cycles each confirmed byte-for-byte deterministic hashes for the five primary generated outputs. A separate existing Mind Tree structural-contract test suite passed 21/21 synthetic tests (see the Mind Tree and verification reports); that validates only the pre-existing validator's synthetic contract, not real Kanji facts or relation correctness.
+
+**Readiness:** grammar-only local materialization and deterministic structural ETL are technically demonstrated. Source provenance is incomplete at author/example level; all records need qualified review; duplicate-pattern interpretation is unresolved; cross-reference coverage is zero; canonical schema mapping is incomplete; broader dataset source availability and rights are unresolved; application integration counts are unknown; K0.13 remains blocked; Windows checks are outstanding. No source-specific restriction, project-use gate, or publication authorization was weakened.
