+# K0.14 ETL and Determinism Report
+
+## Implemented pipeline
+
+`scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py` provides three explicit local commands:
+
+1. `acquire` fetches only the five pinned OpenJLPT grammar JSON files and four license/notice/README artifacts at commit `c42fd9fa3777bfc1775446f7c418d549dfd6e4cf`; verifies byte size, Git blob identity and SHA-256; writes only under Git-ignored `data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/source/` plus `acquisition-manifest.json`.
+2. `build` parses the five files, retains source fields and adds normalized values and field-level provenance, performs structural/example/tag/level checks, reports duplicates and review needs, then writes normalized, quality, reject, duplicate, review-queue and build-manifest JSON under the same ignored local data root.
+3. `verify` rebuilds deterministically and compares the five primary data outputs byte-for-byte. The build manifest itself includes a build timestamp, so it is evidence/metadata rather than one of the five byte-identical payloads.
+
+The source pin and exact file SHA-256 values are recorded in `data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/source/acquisition-manifest.json`; the output hashes and transform version are recorded in `data/k014/openjlpt/v0.2.0/build/build-manifest.json`. A narrow `/data/k014/` rule was added to `.gitignore` after inspection, keeping the raw source and generated data outside Git; the ETL and tests remain regular worktree paths.
+
+## Validation and duplicate/rejection policy
+
+- Source/parsed/normalized/structurally valid: 100/100/100/100.
+- Rejected: 0. Rejection reporting is implemented; empty output is `[]`.
+- Exact duplicate records: 0.
+- Normalized pattern-key collision: 1 between candidate IDs `olp-v0.2.0-n4-0010` and `olp-v0.2.0-n3-0019`. Both are retained; collision is diagnostic, not an automatic merge or rejection.
+- Levels: N1–N5 each 20; all 100 source level values match the containing file.
+- Examples: 200 object values; exactly 2 per source record; all have nonempty `ja` and `en` keys.
+- Tags: 160 tag occurrences and 100 distinct nonempty values.
+- Review queue: 100 items; all `PENDING`; reviewer and timestamp unset; expected corrections null; reason codes include human review and unmapped example origin; each item carries source artifact/hash/locator evidence; publication state `NOT_AUTHORIZED`.
+- Semantic, linguistic, human, and cross-reference validation: not performed / zero coverage. No accuracy claim is made.
+
+Normalization is additive: NFC plus outer whitespace trim, with original source values preserved. Deduplication is diagnostic only. Candidate IDs are local transformation IDs, not upstream IDs.
+
+## Commands and observed results
+
+Acquisition was run once for this pinned snapshot:
+
+```text
+python3 -B scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py acquire
+```
+
+The focused Python tests were run after the review-queue additions:
+
+```text
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_k014_openjlpt_grammar.py' -v
+```
+
+Result: **4 tests passed**. Coverage includes pinned-source checksums, real-source structural/shape counts without semantic claims, a synthetic validator edge case, additive Unicode normalization, level/example/provenance counts and review-queue population.
+
+Two fresh build/verify cycles were run:
+
+```text
+python3 -B scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py build
+python3 -B scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py verify
+python3 -B scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py build
+python3 -B scripts/k014_openjlpt_grammar.py verify
+```
+
+Both `verify` commands returned `PASS`, `byteForByteDeterministicOutputs: true`, and verified exactly `duplicates.json`, `normalized.json`, `quality-report.json`, `rejected.json` and `review-queue.json`. Both reported source 100, normalized 100, rejected 0 and integrated count `UNKNOWN_NOT_CHECKED; no database or CMS accessed`. Both builds reported the same normalized payload SHA-256 `223adb7131e8c2a26b2ddec5961abd4f670a9f117f2cdc8d7d693210649a1fb3` (581,414 bytes).
+
+Final primary output hashes:
+
+| Output | Bytes | SHA-256 |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `normalized.json` | 581,414 | `223adb7131e8c2a26b2ddec5961abd4f670a9f117f2cdc8d7d693210649a1fb3` |
+| `quality-report.json` | 2,984 | `7dc5940991863467abc2af8f993fd146d2a4168abc61f693f35f7ead548058ea` |
+| `rejected.json` | 3 | `37517e5f3dc66819f61f5a7bb8ace1921282415f10551d2defa5c3eb0985b570` |
+| `duplicates.json` | 245 | `bc7066c2074d871c06cd43cfebb3f6ed6faf90abb60c77a11cb4717cd87ef0e6` |
+| `review-queue.json` | 131,408 | `d9581f7ce8fea4b6936aed29551bd67d3f7cbc241e6375ebcd9b1288d44052f2` |
+
+An earlier diagnostic-only ad hoc printer used a nonexistent quality-report key and raised `KeyError`; it did not affect the successful build/verify runs. Refreshed values above were read using the actual `exactDuplicateRecordCount` key. The later test/build/verify sequence passed in full.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+No application ETL, canonical loader, database, CMS, production seed, migration, or API was invoked. The implementation does not ingest other OpenJLPT families or any JMdict, KANJIDIC2, KanjiVG, Tatoeba or WordNet rows. A successful deterministic transform establishes neither source/project authorization nor source correctness, semantic accuracy, canonical compatibility, human review or publication readiness.
