+# NIHONGOBRIDGE — PHASE K0.2
+## Comprehensive Hybrid 2,501-Kanji Selection Policy & Reproducible Membership Design
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-02
+**Verdict:** **PASS WITH CONDITIONS** for policy design; **BLOCKED** for licensing clearance and final candidate derivation.
+**Scope:** evidence review and policy design only. This report is not a membership list, final manifest, approval to ingest, or database authorization.
+
+### Evidence labels used throughout
+
+- **VERIFIED** — directly inspected in this checkout or exact, hash-verified source bytes.
+- **REPORTED** — present in an earlier repository report or source notice; not independently revalidated against the original source in this task.
+- **INFERRED** — a proposed interpretation or policy consequence; owner review required.
+- **UNRESOLVED** — the evidence is incomplete or a policy choice is still needed.
+- **BLOCKED** — a named prerequisite prevents safe approval or distribution.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive verdict
+
+**PASS WITH CONDITIONS.** The four owner-selected objectives can be represented by a single stable membership set with multi-label evidence and separate learning/search views. This report specifies a source-pinned candidate method, a no-weight categorical ranking framework, exact-count stop conditions, Unicode identity rules, baseline disposition, manifest design, approval workflow, and future validation gates.
+
+**The 2,501-character corpus is not selected or ready to freeze.** Direct inspection of the pinned KANJIDIC2 XML resolves an important uncertainty from K0.1: the artifact really does contain 2,501 distinct characters carrying `<freq>` values, with each serialized rank 1–2,501 present exactly once. That field is a newspaper-based ordinal frequency ranking, not a universal modern reading corpus or an owner-approved membership definition. It omits 10,607 of the 13,108 source records, including 99 records coded as Jōyō education grade; its 2,501 frequency-tagged characters include 464 outside the Jōyō grade-coded set. Using the frequency subset as the owner’s corpus would therefore not implement the approved four-objective hybrid.
+
+A defensible default is: **pin and include the complete official Jōyō literacy core, then select one ranked extension from explicitly approved frequency, education/learner, name, specialist and real-text evidence.** The number of extension slots is a consequence of `2,501 − verified core size`, not a quota to be divided among objectives. Objective labels may overlap on one identity. The exact extension precedence must be approved before a deterministic run; the evidence cannot supply a neutral ordering between incomparable goals without adding an arbitrary weight or priority.
+
+**KANJIDIC2 licensing is precisely BLOCKED, not silently resolved.** Local M3 records the current EDRDG notice as CC BY-SA 4.0 superseding prior wording, while the historical source contract/manifest still say CC BY-SA 3.0. The exact pinned archive contains no license file and links to EDRDG’s licence page. A direct retrieval of that primary page failed in this environment; do not rely on a GitHub repository-level license badge as a substitute. The source declaration most recently recorded in-repo is 4.0, but a qualified owner/legal reviewer must verify its applicability to this exact 2023-08 artifact and derived outputs before distribution clearance.
+
+No source code, canonical records, source datasets in the repository, database contents, migrations, or production systems were changed. The exact pinned KANJIDIC2 artifact was downloaded transiently to `/tmp` for byte verification and read-only analysis; it was not added to the repository.
+
+## 2. Exact repository and gate identity
+
+### 2.1 Checkout identity at opening inspection
