+### 11.1 Manifest fields
+
+Top-level machine-readable fields:
+
+- `manifestId`: stable corpus identifier.
+- `schemaVersion`: manifest schema version.
+- `corpusVersion`: immutable corpus revision; distinct from schema version.
+- `targetCount`: integer exactly `2501` after approval.
+- `identityPolicy`: Unicode version, eligible identity class, one-scalar rule, normalization, variant/IVS rules and identity-generator version.
+- `selectionPolicy`: policy ID/version/digest, objective definitions, core source, extension evidence tiers, categorical precedence and deterministic ordering tuple.
+- `sourceLock`: each source ID, title, version/date, immutable URL/commit, source file/path, size, SHA-256/Git blob where applicable, field semantics, license notice ID/version, attribution, use decision and reviewer reference.
+- `entries`: ordered by numeric scalar value, one per unique identity.
+- `decisionLedger`: companion candidate decision artifact ID/version/hash, including included, excluded, deferred, quarantined, duplicate-source and exception decisions.
+- `createdAt`, `createdBy`, `generatorVersion`, `policyApprovedAt`, `sourceApprovedAt`, `membershipApprovedAt`, `frozenAt`: fixed ISO-8601 UTC timestamps and named approver role/identity references. Do not stamp a new generation time into the same frozen bytes.
+- `reviewState`: `CANDIDATE`, `EVIDENCE_CHECKED`, `POLICY_REVIEWED`, `APPROVED`, `FROZEN`.
+- `supersedes`: prior `manifestId`, `corpusVersion` and SHA-256, null only for initial version.
+- `canonicalization`: version and exact serialization/hash rules.
+- `manifestSha256`: digest of canonical manifest body excluding only this digest field; approval attestations are detached and reference this hash.
+
+Each `entries[]` item:
+
+- `ordinal`, exact `character`, numeric `codePoint`/`U+XXXX`, stable code-point-derived `canonicalId`.
+- `inclusionCategories[]` (multi-valued objective/source labels, not quotas), `selectionRuleId`, concise inclusion rationale.
+- `evidence[]`: `sourceId`, source release, artifact hash, record key/path, field/tag, raw value, field interpretation/version, extraction method/version, evidence status and reviewer decision. Raw claims must be distinguishable from derived summaries.
+- `relationships[]`: typed variant/alias/historical/glyph/IVS relations with exact target code point, relation source, direction and approval status.
+- `sourceCoverage`: per-source state (`present`, `missing`, `unavailable`, `not_applicable`, `not_reviewed`, `conflict`, `quarantined`) and relevant artifact/record key. Missing evidence is never a fabricated value.
+- `baselineReconciliation`: existing Mind Tree/pilot source ID and ID if applicable; `included`, `outside_policy_preserved`, `identity_conflict` or `pending_review`. Do not use this field to authorize deletion.
+- `reviewState`, reviewer role/ID, decision time, rationale and exception reference.
