+## 12. Candidate review, owner approvals and state transitions
+
+### 12.1 Candidate lifecycle
+
+`CANDIDATE → EVIDENCE_CHECKED → POLICY_REVIEWED → APPROVED → FROZEN`
+
+Additional terminal/holding states: `REJECTED`, `DEFERRED`, `QUARANTINED`.
+
+- `CANDIDATE`: exact scalar and candidate source row registered, not a membership claim.
+- `EVIDENCE_CHECKED`: source digest/field/raw value verified and identity/variant relation validated. Missing values remain explicit.
+- `POLICY_REVIEWED`: inclusion/exclusion rule and objective labels reviewed; candidate cutoff and other objectives are visible.
+- `APPROVED`: named authority approves the individual candidate or approved rule-based cohort after seeing the full ledger. A rule-level approval must list its exact source query/version and exceptions.
+- `FROZEN`: included candidate appears exactly once in the frozen manifest; ledger and manifest digest are published internally read-only.
+- `REJECTED`: evidence establishes it fails a stated eligibility rule; preserve the reason and source row.
+- `DEFERRED`: evidence/policy decision is pending; not counted or silently replaced.
+- `QUARANTINED`: identity, variant, provenance or license conflict; cannot be approved until resolved.
+
+Every accepted, excluded, deferred, quarantined or exceptional candidate receives an auditable reason. A dispute at the 2,501 cutoff halts freeze; do not accept it just to reach the target.
